      R. Q. 2 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَكَأْكَأَ</span></b>  <i>He was prevented,</i> or <i>hindered.</i>
(Lth.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَكَأْكَأَ فِى كَلَامِهِ</span> <i>He hesitated in his
speech, and was unable to speak.</i> (K.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2- 
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَكَأْكَأَ عَلَيْهِ النَّاسُ</span>, (S, K, *) and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كَأْكَأَ</span></b> , (K,) <i>The
people collected around him;</i> (S, K;) <i>crowded,</i>
or <i>pressed, upon him.</i> (TA.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A3-  And see R. Q. 1.

